cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below, and record the exact commit you used.
title: 'ScalarPitchfork: scalar pitchfork bifurcation with a jet-bounded remainder and the topology of global branches in Lean 4'
type: software
authors:
- family-names: Chen
  given-names: Le
  affiliation: Auburn University
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/chenle02/scalar-pitchfork-lean
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 library on the scalar pitchfork normal form f(tau, z) = alpha tau z - beta z^3 + R(tau, z)
  with a remainder bounded by explicit weights. It proves that for small parameters on the side
  tau beta > 0 there are exactly two small nontrivial zeros, one of each sign, given by branch
  functions continuous in the parameter, with amplitude sqrt(alpha tau / beta) up to an explicit
  O(|tau|) error and with the stability sign of beta, and that there are none on the other side. The
  remainder bounds follow from C^4 smoothness, vanishing on the axis and five vanishing jets at the
  origin; a stronger bound holds if and only if an axis condition holds, and the jets alone do not
  imply it. The global part proves the topological skeleton of global bifurcation alternatives, with
  the alternatives as hypotheses: a non-compact component has unbounded parameter, and the one-sided
  component is closed.
keywords:
- Lean 4
- Mathlib
- formalization
- bifurcation theory
- pitchfork bifurcation
- normal form
- global bifurcation
- connected components
